# finish/glyph: T6's light laid INTO the filigree on P (STYLE_P2 27.3, 27.7; LADDER-FINISH, ladder slice i3): the oak's
# VEIN turned to light (! Glow 2, : Glow 3, ^ Glow 4: absolute, light is light): the badge's vein on a cloak's back, the
# leaf under a shield's boss, a pauldron leaf's vein; a row of staves on a brow band. Breastplate panels (2x2, 2x3) carry
# none (a lone glyph pixel there read as a speck; the chest gem and the seam runes light it). i2's algiz read as a "T".
# Stacks over finish/filigree (a clear cell falls through to the gold), so T6 = T5's gold with the writing glowing in it:
# the T6 still reads by day at 1x, and the breath (27.7) moves real area. FIT-centred like the filigree.
# Generated by LADDER-FINISH's gen_finish.py.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.glyph
legend ! glow 2
legend : glow 3
legend ^ glow 4
tags tile overlay fit
on-region P

